WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.937
Welcome to Projectile Motion.

2
00:00:02.887 --> 00:00:05.975
Today we master The Max Height Arc.

3
00:00:05.975 --> 00:00:17.187
According to NCERT: At maximum height, the vertical component of velocity is zero while horizontal velocity remains v0*cos(theta).

4
00:00:17.187 --> 00:00:25.200
The primary formula is: H max = (v naught squared * sin^2(θ)) / (2g).

5
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:35.050
Notice this crucial insight: HCV Ch 3: Speed at the top is not zero; it equals v0*cos(theta).

6
00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.662
Kinetic energy is minimum but non-zero.

7
00:00:38.662 --> 00:00:50.225
Pay special attention to this NEET trap point: Confusing total velocity being zero with only vertical velocity component being zero at top of trajectory.

8
00:00:50.225 --> 00:00:55.937
Keep this core relationship firmly in mind to secure top marks in NEET.

9
00:00:55.937 --> 00:01:01.600
Up next in video 5: Horizontal Range and Complementary Angles.
